    "body": "## Overview\n\nRemoves the dead `chunk_size_in_s` variable from `SpeechToTextServing._create_speech_to_text` in `vllm/entrypoints/speech_to_text/base/serving.py`. This is one of the leftover cleanups from #32588 (follow-up to #41131).\n\n## Claims\n\n- `chunk_size_in_s` was assigned from `self.asr_config.max_audio_clip_s` but never read anywhere — it is removed.\n- No behavior change: the `assert` that sat under the variable checks a real invariant (chunking disabled → exactly one result generator), so it is kept, reading the config directly instead of through the dead variable.\n- Scope is deliberately limited to the dead code. The two docstring leftovers from #32588 are already covered by #49414, so they are not duplicated here.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `grep` over the codebase confirms no remaining references to `chunk_size_in_s`; the variable had exactly one assignment and zero reads.\n- The edited file compiles (`py_compile`) and the diff is a single condition line: `if chunk_size_in_s is None:` → `if self.asr_config.max_audio_clip_s is None:`, with the dead assignment deleted.\n- No new tests: this is a dead-code removal with no behavior change, so there is no observable behavior to assert. Relying on CI for the existing speech-to-text test coverage.\n\n## Details\n\n#41131 switched speech-to-text chunk timestamps to a cumulative approach, after which `chunk_size_in_s` stopped being used but was left behind. Thanks to @Asthenia0412 for identifying this and the other leftovers in #32588.\n\nDesign decision worth noting: an earlier draft of this cleanup (on the reporter's fork) removed the whole `if` block including the assert. I kept the assert because it guards a genuine invariant — if `max_audio_clip_s` is `None`, audio cannot be chunked, so merging more than one result generator would be a bug. Removing the variable does not require weakening that check.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
